  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A diffraction grating with grating spacing <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\"></span> is illuminated normally using a beam of monochromatic light of wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span>. The angle between the straight-through position and the first order maximum is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\alpha\"></span> and the angle between the first order and the second order maxima is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\beta\"></span>. What is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{asin\\alpha}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{asin\\beta}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{asin(\\alpha + \\beta)}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{asin(\\alpha - \\beta)}{2}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
